toolContracts.description:
Check an HTML page before html_render. Returns PNG, contentHeight, and console output. If it says the browser is still installing, call again in a minute. Inline <style> and <script>. Local images as absolute paths are inlined. Remote URLs load as-is. Theme and layout rules are in html_render.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__t3_code__html_preview(args: {
  // Default dark.
  appearance?: "dark" | "light";
  // A complete, self-contained HTML document.
  html: string;
  // CSS pixels, 240 to 1600. Default 728. Use about 390 for phones.
  width?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Show a finished HTML page (chart, diagram, mockup) inline in this thread, above your final reply. Do not announce or restate the page. Frame fits height to 20000px. On mobile, content past the given height scrolls. Frame width is reply width (728px desktop, about 360px phones), on the thread background. Leave html, body, and the outer element with no background color, no outer card, border, banner title, or side padding. This wins over any rule that sets a page background. T3 adds an overridable 8px html gutter for selection rings and shadows. Use fluid widths within it. A box that needs its own background gets 16px padding and var(--radius) corners. Give charts fixed pixel heights. Let content set the height. Do not use vh units or height:100% on html or body. Both are rejected or loop. Use theme CSS variables on :root, not fixed colors: --background, --foreground, --muted, --card, --popover, --secondary, --border, --ring, --primary, --accent, --destructive, --warning, --success, --info, --code-background (most have a matching -foreground; accent, destructive, and warning also have -surface), --chart-1 to --chart-6, --radius, --font-sans, --font-mono. The base sheet sets background, text, and font.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__t3_code__html_render(args: {
  // Frame height in CSS pixels, 80 to 2000. Use the contentHeight from html_preview.
  height: number;
  // A complete, self-contained HTML document.
  html: string;
  title: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ htmlRender: { attachmentId: string; height: number | "Infinity" | "-Infinity" | "NaN"; heights?: Array<[number, number]> | null; title: string; [key: string]: unknown; }; message: string; [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };
```

Open a preview tab in this thread and show it. For a dev server, pass `target` instead of `url`. `open=false` keeps it in the background. Reuses your current tab unless `tabId` or `reuseExistingTab=false` says otherwise. Parallel subagents in one session must each use `reuseExistingTab=false`, then their own returned `tabId`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__t3_code__preview_open(args: {
  // Show the preview to the user. Default true. False for background only.
  open?: boolean;
  // Profile id or name from preview_status, for a new tab. Default: the user's. A tab keeps its profile.
  profileId?: string;
  // Reuse `tabId`, or your current tab. Default true. False makes a new tab.
  reuseExistingTab?: boolean;
  // Old alias for `open`.
  show?: boolean;
  tabId?: string;
  target?: {
  kind: "environment-port";
  // Path, query, and fragment, such as /settings?tab=account.
  path?: string;
  // Dev-server port here.
  port: number;
  // Default http.
  protocol?: "http" | "https";
};
  // First page URL. Absolute http(s) URL, or a bare host (https; http for loopback). Omit to open a blank tab.
  url?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{ available: boolean; control?: { generation: number | "Infinity" | "-Infinity" | "NaN"; ownedByCaller: boolean; owner: "agent" | "human" | "unclaimed"; [key: string]: unknown; } | null; defaultProfileId?: string | null; dialog?: { defaultValue: string; message: string; type: string; [key: string]: unknown; } | null | null; downloads?: Array<{ completedAt: string; fileName: string; path: string; sizeBytes: number | "Infinity" | "-Infinity" | "NaN"; url: string; [key: string]: unknown; }> | null; fileChooser?: { accept: string; multiple: boolean; [key: string]: unknown; } | null | null; loading: boolean; profiles?: Array<{ id: string; incognito?: boolean | null; name: string; [key: string]: unknown; }> | null; tabId: string | null; tabs?: Array<{ openerTabId?: string | null; ownedByCaller?: boolean | null; owner?: "agent" | "human" | "unclaimed" | null; profileId?: string | null; tabId: string; url: string | null; visible?: boolean | null; [key: string]: unknown; }> | null; title: string | null; url: string | null; viewport?: { height: number; width: number; [key: string]: unknown; } | null; viewportSetting?: { _tag: "fill"; [key: string]: unknown; } | { _tag: "freeform"; height: number; width: number; [key: string]: unknown; } | { _tag: "preset"; height: number; presetId: "iphone-se" | "iphone-xr" | "iphone-12-pro" | "iphone-14-pro-max" | "pixel-7" | "samsung-galaxy-s8-plus" | "samsung-galaxy-s20-ultra" | "ipad-mini" | "ipad-air" | "ipad-pro" | "surface-pro-7" | "surface-duo" | "galaxy-z-fold-5" | "asus-zenbook-fold" | "samsung-galaxy-a51-71" | "nest-hub" | "nest-hub-max" | "desktop-1920x1080" | "desktop-1440x900" | "laptop-1366x768" | "laptop-1280x800" | "ipad-pro-11" | "iphone-15-pro" | "pixel-8" | "galaxy-s24"; width: number; [key: string]: unknown; } | null; visible: boolean; [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };
